  :adr/body
  "## What was measured

All **2,098** `kotoba-lang` entries in `manifest/west.yml`, each compared
against its child repository's **remote** default-branch head via the GitHub
API — never against a local checkout, since `main`, the pin and the checkout are
three different things.

- 406 already current
- **1,692 behind**, every one `status: ahead`, `behind_by: 0`,
  `merge_base == pin` — **strict fast-forwards**
- **0 diverged, 0 unreachable, 0 unmeasurable**

## What the lag actually was

**1,627 of the 1,692 (97%) had the identical tip commit:**
`chore(license): Apache-2.0 (kotoba-lang org-wide unification)`.

A license sweep ran across the org and the manifest was never advanced behind
it. So a fresh `west update`, and every fleet CI run, read trees **without the
licence those repositories are published under**. Nothing failed; nothing
reported it; the pins simply pointed one commit before the sweep, 1,627 times.

The other 47 carried real work a stale pin was hiding: kotobase engine
`bounded-manifest-v2` and `logical-canonical-v1`, `db.unique/value` enforcement,
secp256k1 verify, Mach-O relocations, a `social/publish` capability, PNG encode,
OpenType cmap.

**1,674 pins were advanced**, in 16 batches, each passing
`verify-west-pins.cljs`. Independent re-measure after landing: 0 still at the
old pin; 1,672 at exactly the measured head and 2 advanced further by concurrent
sessions. A fresh sweep now reads 2,080 / 2,098 current, and the 18 still behind
are exactly the declared exclusions.

## The 18 not advanced, and why each is a decision rather than an oversight

- **`compiler`** (58 behind) — redirects to `kotoba-lang/amu`, which west
  already registers separately. One repository at two paths: manifest hygiene,
  not a pin refresh. This is the open retirement question.
- **`com-unity-api-services`** — default branch is
  `rescue/uncommitted-mcp-adapter-20260725`. Advancing would pin the manifest
  onto someone's rescue branch.
- **`kotoba-pages-poc`** — default branch is `gh-pages`, build output.
- **5 × `kami-engine-*`** — group `archived`, excluded by `group-filter`.
- **`emr-claims-primary-sources`** — group `datalad`; pin changes have custody
  implications.
- **9 × `kotoba-lang-{bim,cad,ekyc,kenchi,sha256d,states,svgraph,tenso,yotei}`**
  — a tooling gap, now fixed. See below.

## Two defects in `advance-pins.cljs`, both now closed

### It could not advance an entry whose `name` differs from its path

The 9 above are registered as `kotoba-lang-bim` at `orgs/kotoba-lang/bim`, and
the script looked up HEAD by `name` only. All 9 404 on GitHub. It failed *safe*
— wrote nothing — but **silently**, so the entries were simply unreachable by
the tool that exists to advance them.

It now falls back to the last segment of the entry's `path:` and prints
`resolved via path segment <x>` when it does. All 9 advanced and verified
fast-forward in this change.

### It swallowed rate-limit failures and exited 0

`head-sha` caught every exception and returned `nil`, so a repository that does
not exist, a name that is not the repository's path, and a rate limit all became
the same `:no-sha` count — and the script succeeded regardless.

**Measured: with the shared hourly budget exhausted, 210 lookups failed, the
script reported `:no-sha 210`, wrote nothing, and exited 0.** A run that touched
no pin at all, indistinguishable from a run where those repositories were gone.

Now there are two outcomes, not one: a 40-hex string, or an error that is kept,
printed with its slug, and **exits 1**. Proven both ways with a `gh` on PATH
that exits 1 — the old script exits 0, this one exits 1 and names each failure.

The response is also shape-checked. Anything that is not 40 hex characters is
refused rather than written, because **a 403 JSON body was very nearly
interpolated into `west.yml` as a revision today** by a caller that did not
check.

**This is the third instance of one bug class in a single day**, after
`verify-duplicate-registrations --verify-remote` and my own ADR validator: a
check whose failure is reported but does not stop anything. The shape is always
the same — the tool answers its own question correctly, the caller draws a wider
conclusion, and nothing refuses.

## A premise of my own that was a stale read

The brief for this audit said `orgs/kotoba-lang/amu` is checked out at `8ff1030`
**ahead** of its west pin. Wrong in both halves: the pin was **already current**
at `488cd12c` in local and `origin/main` west.yml, and the checkout is **77
commits behind the pin**, not ahead. The pin had been advanced since the
observation I quoted. Nothing to do on the manifest; the local checkout is stale
and carries 5 modified files, untouched.

## Operational notes

Batches had to be ~100 pins: the Bash tool caps at 10 minutes and advance+verify
for 210 overran it. Each batch needs sync-and-apply in one call and commit in
the next, because the verify guard is a PreToolUse hook that inspects the tree
*before* the command runs. Four retries were needed where concurrent sessions
advanced unrelated pins mid-batch — re-synced and re-applied each time, never
rebased, never forced."}]
